From f7eeda127100fa30c9bb5ef96bf758494717c38e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fefi-byte <55361862+fefi-byte@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:50:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] op2-sim: a path order waiting for the unit's turn leaves
 the old path context in place

The packet fills the second path context (+0x38); the unit's own (+0x34) stays until its turn swaps them (0x44B640).
Until then the bump (0x44BCB0) reads the old path's next step and turning state, a Stop restores the old waypoints, a
side-step taken before the turn is dropped with the old context, and an idle unit with its Move context still there
goes back to its waypoint. A Stop keeps the steps as well; a running side-step of an earthworker stays.
Measured against the original in the Wine harness: mp2_05 seed 1 (tanks 54, 65, 66, 67), mp2_08 seed 1 (Lynx 57,
Spider 49), mp4_12 seed 3 (Earthworker 53).

Written with Claude Code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
